# Tacit's live system and what the installer copies onto a disk: added to archiso's baseline profile's list.
# hardware
linux-firmware
intel-ucode
amd-ucode
sof-firmware
mesa
vulkan-intel
vulkan-radeon
intel-media-driver
# the desktop
tacit
tacit-thyris
tacit-keyring
sddm
# the keyring the lock opens at login (Thyris keeps passwords in it; it refuses a plain one)
gnome-keyring
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji
# Chinese, Japanese and Korean text (pages showed boxes without them)
noto-fonts-cjk
ttf-dejavu
hunspell-en_us
hunspell-en_gb
networkmanager
bluez
bluez-utils
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
wireplumber
sudo
# what the installer uses
arch-install-scripts
squashfs-tools
gptfdisk
parted
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
# next to Windows: ntfsresize shrinks it, ntfscat reads whether it is hibernated
ntfsprogs
efibootmgr
# cameras: Tacit's libcamera (sensor helpers stock lacks) and PipeWire's camera plugin; the GTK portal answers the
# camera permission (xdg-desktop-portal's Access) until Tacit's own portal does
libcamera
libcamera-ipa
pipewire-libcamera
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
# more hardware (2026-10-16): NVIDIA's open driver (Turing and newer; the installer drops it where there is no NVIDIA
# card), old Broadcom Wi-Fi, printing (CUPS, printers found on the network), firmware updates, Thunderbolt docks,
# fingerprint readers, the rotation sensor of 2-in-1s
nvidia-open
nvidia-utils
# old Broadcom Wi-Fi: Arch ships the driver as DKMS, built against the kernel's headers when the image is made
broadcom-wl-dkms
linux-headers
cups
avahi
fwupd
bolt
fprintd
iio-sensor-proxy
